# What differs from run to run of PostgreSQL's suite with the same settings
# (differential.py): a regular expression a line, its groups replaced; "!" a
# line dropped; "@test" one test's alone.
#
# The gpu session (differential.sh, V8): the explain test's plan of a
# parallel sort, handed as rows (jsonb_pretty), says whether the leader's
# VecSort sorted on the device or passed work_mem first and handed its kept
# rows to tuplesort, by how much of the table the leader read, run by run --
# as the test drops core's Sort Method for.  Those lines dropped, the comma of
# the line before them marked, and psql's padding to the widest line marked:
# the header's, the separator's and each line's before its "+".
@explain !"Device": "
@explain !"Kept Rows Put into tuplesort":
@explain "Shared Written Blocks": 0(,?) *\+?$
@explain ^ +jsonb_pretty *$
@explain ^(-+)$
@explain [^ ]( +)\+$
